Skill: Operating manual for Spec-Symphony orchestrator. Read BEFORE any stage work.

Keywords: spec-kit, openspec, SDD, workflow, orchestration, spawn contract, remote runner, execute_series, note, github webhook, linear.

========================================================================
0) Reality check — stage orchestrator, not shell executor
========================================================================

You **do** execute the workflow: each stage is your job — parse the trigger, `note()` handoff keys, spawn **approved** subagents, close with `stage_summary`.

You are **not** the shell executor. You **CANNOT** call `${shell_tool_prefix}_execute_*` yourself. Clone, validate, commit, and `gh` run inside **spawned subagents** on remote runner `${remote_runner_name}`.

When this SOP says "run clone" or "call gh", spawn ONE approved subagent from the stage spawn contracts. Copy spawn-context command lines **verbatim** into `execute_series`.

**FORBIDDEN subagent names:** `retry-*`, `recovery-*`, `*-v2`, `verify-*`, or any name not listed on the stage spawn_contracts. Guild rejects unknown names ("tools not available in tool registry"). On failure, re-spawn the **same** contract name (e.g. `intake-clone-bootstrap-clone`) — never invent `retry-intake-clone-bootstrap-clone`.

========================================================================
0a) Remote runner must be online BEFORE shell work
========================================================================

`${shell_tool_prefix}_execute_series` talks to aiden-runner over RPC. If the runner container is not running or not connected:
- Tool returns instantly with no stdout
- Subagent sees `context canceled` / `adaptive loop interrupted`
- Clone never runs; notes stay `{}`

**Operator fix:** `tofu apply` then `./scripts/start-runner.sh --run` (or Helm equivalent) **before** firing the webhook. After script-pack changes, restart the runner for secret sync.

When clone subagent hits `context canceled` or empty tool output:
1. **Retry** the same spawn-context clone command up to **3 times** with **15s** backoff (`infra_retry=<n>`).
2. After retries exhausted: `note` `clone_blocker=runner_unavailable`
3. Echo `stage_summary:intake-clone-bootstrap=blocked: remote runner offline or RPC failed`
4. STOP — `intake-blocked-gate` routes to `create-pr` for blocker comment.

**Operator:** After `tofu apply` or runner restart, wait ~30s before webhook (`./scripts/start-runner.sh --run` then sleep) so aiden-runner connects.

========================================================================
0b) Trigger payload is the source of truth
========================================================================

GitHub/Linear webhooks arrive as prose in stage Input:

```
opened: {"action":"opened","issue":{"number":64,...},"repository":{"full_name":"org/repo","clone_url":"https://github.com/org/repo.git",...}}
```

**Also read `[Workflow execution]` header** for `workflow_run_id` → `note workflow_run_id`. For shell commands use spawn-header **`WORK_ROOT='{{work_root}}'`** verbatim — **FORBIDDEN:** `$HOME/.wf-*`, `$HOME}/`, or manual path concatenation.

**In `intake-clone-bootstrap` (mandatory before clone subagent):**
1. Copy `workflow_run_id` → `note workflow_run_id`
2. Parse JSON from Input (text after first `": "`). Do not rely only on `trigger_event.payload.*` (often empty).
3. `note()` exact keys:
   - `repository.full_name` → `repository_full_name`
   - `repository.clone_url` → `repository_clone_url`
   - `repository.default_branch` → `repository_default_branch`
   - `issue.number` or `pull_request.number` → `issue_or_pr_number` (e.g. `64` — never leave empty when issue exists)
   - `issue.title`, `issue.body` → compact `issue_details` JSON
   - `issue.labels[].name` → `issue_labels`
   - webhook `action` → `event_type`
   - `sdd_framework=${sdd_framework}`, `change_type=${change_type}`
4. If parsing fails, `note stage_summary:intake-clone-bootstrap=blocked: unparseable webhook` and STOP.

========================================================================
0c) GitHub auth on runner
========================================================================

PAT syncs to runner via `typed_secret_refs.github` (`GIT_TOKEN`, `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`). Shell subagents use pack `${specsym_pack_dir}/clone-pack.sh` — do not hand-roll `git clone` URLs.

**FORBIDDEN:** `gh auth token`, persisting tokens in notes. If `gh_env_present=false` and clone fails for private repo → `clone_blocker=auth`, blocked intake.

========================================================================
1) Workflow shape — spec-driven-feature
========================================================================

```
intake-clone-bootstrap → intake-blocked-gate → repo-sdd-bootstrap → implement → implement-blocked-gate → validate-and-test → validate-loop-gate → create-pr → update-tracker
```

**Intake fast-path (`intake-blocked-gate`):** clone/runner failure → skip to **`create-pr`** (blocker comment).

**Implement fast-path (`implement-blocked-gate`):** plan-only / `implement_blocker=*` → skip to **`create-pr`**.

**Quality loop (`validate-loop-gate` only):** `output_matches_regex` exits on `module_quality_summary=PASS|BLOCKED`; GO_BACK to `implement` on `NEEDS_REVISION` (max ${quality_max_iterations}). **`validate-and-test` is agent-only** — never `loop_stage` (trace `e22cc371`).

**Post-PR (`update-tracker`):** optional OpenSpec archive, then GitHub issue comment / Linear notify.

========================================================================
2) Stage-boundary spawn rules (hard)
========================================================================

| Stage | Allowed subagents | Forbidden |
|-------|-------------------|-----------|
| `intake-clone-bootstrap` | `intake-clone-bootstrap-clone` | `implement-*`, `validate-*`, `create-pr-*`, `load_skill`, ad-hoc names |
| `repo-sdd-bootstrap` | `repo-sdd-bootstrap-runner` | others |
| `implement` | `implement-spec-feature` | `validate-*`, `create-pr-*` |
| `validate-and-test` | `validate-and-test-runner` | `implement-*`, `create-pr-*` |
| `create-pr` | `create-pr-runner`, `create-pr-notify` | `validate-*`, `implement-*` |
| `update-tracker` | `archive-specs-runner`, `update-tracker-notify` | intake/clone/validate |

Each shell subagent: `task_type=terminal_calling`, ONE `${shell_tool_prefix}_execute_series` per spawn, `working_dir=${shell_work_home}` or omit.

**Shell `$` rule:** single `$` for `$PD`, `$WORK_ROOT`. Never `$$` before variable names (breaks pack base64 decode).

========================================================================
3) Stage note ownership
========================================================================

| Stage | Writes |
|-------|--------|
| `intake-clone-bootstrap` | `repository_*`, `issue_or_pr_number`, `issue_details`, `repo_clone_path`, `repo_head_sha`, `gate_result` |
| `repo-sdd-bootstrap` | `sdd_framework_used`, `spec_bootstrap_summary` |
| `implement` | `implement_summary` |
| `validate-and-test` | `module_quality_summary`, `ci_status`, `validation_summary` |
| `create-pr` | `pr_url`, `working_branch`, `stage_summary:create-pr` |
| `update-tracker` | tracker comment evidence |

Close every stage with `stage_summary:<stage_id>=done` or `=blocked: <reason>`.

========================================================================
4) SDD frameworks (module default: ${sdd_framework})
========================================================================

- **spec-kit** (greenfield): `.specify/`, `specs/NNN-feature/`, plan.md, tasks.md
- **openspec** (brownfield): `openspec/changes/<id>/` with proposal.md, tasks.md, delta specs
- **ai-dlc** (AWS AI-DLC ${aidlc_rules_version}): `aidlc-docs/<id>/` with inception.md, construction.md, operations.md; tasks in `construction.md`. Seeds `.aidlc-rule-details/` + `AGENTS.md` or `.cursor/rules/ai-dlc-workflow.mdc` from awslabs/aidlc-workflows (fetched at apply). No archive step.

**AI-DLC tenets (when sdd_framework=ai-dlc):**
- Human-in-the-loop: PR review is the approval gate; never auto-merge.
- Question-driven in files: write `## Open Questions` in inception.md and post to issue/Linear — do not block workflow on chat clarifications.
- Adaptive depth: use `change_type` (greenfield = full Inception; bugfix = lean).

`repo-sdd-bootstrap` runs `stage-runner.sh spec-bootstrap` when framework dirs missing.

========================================================================
5) Markers gates depend on (stdout or stage close)
========================================================================

- `clone_blocker=(auth|auth_or_network|network|branch|placeholder_url|runner_unavailable)`
- `stage_summary:intake-clone-bootstrap=blocked`
- `specsym_pack_error=`, `script_pack_error=`
- `context canceled`, `adaptive loop interrupted`
- `module_quality_summary=(PASS|NEEDS_REVISION|BLOCKED)`
- `ci_status=(PASS|FAILED|TIMEOUT|PENDING)`
- `pr_url=`, `implement_blocker=`

========================================================================
6) Failure handling
========================================================================

Blocked clone/auth/runner → intake-blocked-gate → `create-pr` spawns `create-pr-notify` with gh issue comment (no code changes).

At most ONE `ask_clarifying_question` per stage. Never declare workflow success without `repo_clone_path` (unless blocked path taken).
